## Ⅰ. THE 42 SOVEREIGN COGNITIVE LANGUAGES

### Meta-Class: BEING LANGUAGES
```
OCL  — Organism Contract Language        (per-organism charter)
CIL  — Cognitive Internal Language        (inner monologue / self-description)
PIL  — Psyche Internal Language           (subconscious patterns, impulses, drives)
SIL  — Self-Identity Language             (who am I across roles and contexts)
```

### Meta-Class: LAW / CONTRACT LANGUAGES
```
CPL-L — Cognitive Law Language            (constitutions and doctrine)
CPL-C — Cognitive Contract Language       (intelligence contracts)
CPL-P — Cognitive Processing Language     (thought/flow language)
CDL   — Cognitive Doctrine Language       (deep doctrine: philosophy, ethics, metaphysics)
```

### Meta-Class: WORLD LANGUAGES
```
RSL  — Realm Script Language              (world/physics language)
ACL  — Atlas Configuration Language       (ontology/config language)
TPL  — Terminal Protocol Language          (terminal command/event language)
```

### Meta-Class: GROWTH LANGUAGES
```
SPL  — Study Pattern Language             (personal learning blueprints)
EDL  — Educational Doctrine Language      (school/subject doctrine)
PWL  — Pathway Language                   (life/education path language)
TSL  — Tool Scaffold Language             (personal tool-builder language)
WFL  — Work Flow Language                 (how you actually work)
EXL  — Experiment Language                (how you run experiments)
```

### Meta-Class: RELATIONAL LANGUAGES
```
REL  — Relational Ecology Language        (how you relate to people, AIs, orgs)
COL  — Collective Orchestration Language  (how many beings work together)
ROL  — Role Language                      (how roles are defined, swapped, merged)
```

### Meta-Class: MYTH / VALUE / RITUAL LANGUAGES
```
MYL  — Mythic Language                    (trickster, lineage, gods, cosmology)
STL  — Story Thread Language              (arcs: seasons, chapters, sagas)
SYM  — Symbolic Language                  (colors, numbers, shapes, sigils)
VAL  — Value Language                     (what "worth it" means)
RIT  — Ritual Language                    (how transitions are marked)
BOL  — Boundary Language                  (what is allowed where)
GAT  — Gate Language                      (how access is granted/denied)
```

### Meta-Class: DEEP INTERNAL LANGUAGES
```
TIL  — Temporal Integration Language      (past, present, future braiding)
RIL  — Repair & Integration Language      (healing, reconciliation, conflict resolution)
```

### Meta-Class: CREATION / CHAOS LANGUAGES
```
CXL  — Creation Language                  (how new things emerge from nothing)
ERR  — Error Narrative Language           (how failures are told and integrated)
CHL  — Chaos Handling Language            (how anomalies and edge cases are treated)
FRL  — Fringe Language                    (the weirdest stuff: phantoms, auto-encryption)
```

### Economic Stack
```
RCL  — Resource Circulation Language      (how resources move)
GIL  — Gift Language                      (giving without hollowing yourself out)
```

